    {
      "id": "3386af7e-f736-4195-8ddd-1dd1a2640a36",
      "name": "MCP turns tools into useful context",
      "path": "WWW / MCP Notes / MCP turns tools into useful context",
      "docTypeId": "0388f06e-e2df-4366-8282-92ea82871671",
      "templateId": "030812a4-3f8a-44b6-a9b1-4f3cb67d9fcd",
      "state": "Published",
      "domains": [],
      "values": [
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.BlockGrid",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "blocks",
          "value": {
            "layout": {
              "Umbraco.BlockGrid": [
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "22000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
                  "settingsKey": null
                }
              ]
            },
            "contentData": [
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "a32337a5-31e5-4664-88c4-3628398541a6",
                "key": "22000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "heading",
                    "value": "MCP turns tools into useful context"
                  },
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextArea",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "intro",
                    "value": "The Model Context Protocol gives an AI the right context and the right tools, at the point work happens."
                  },
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.MediaPicker3",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "image",
                    "value": [
                      {
                        "key": "22000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
                        "mediaKey": "db0db6b3-68cf-40b2-bff5-8a6575461d57",
                        "mediaTypeAlias": "Image",
                        "crops": [],
                        "focalPoint": null
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.RichText",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "body",
                    "value": {
                      "markup": "<p>MCP is awesome because it replaces a pile of one-off integrations with a clear contract between an AI client and a capable server.</p><p>Instead of pasting data between tabs, a server can safely expose the precise actions and read models that matter: inspect a content tree, create an image, or publish a page. The result is less context switching and more work that can be checked.</p><p>For a CMS, that means an agent can understand the schema before it creates content, use the same management API as the backoffice, and verify the exact document it wrote.</p>",
                      "blocks": {
                        "layout": {},
                        "contentData": [],
                        "settingsData": [],
                        "expose": []
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "settingsData": [],
            "expose": [
              {
                "contentKey": "22000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
                "culture": null,
                "segment": null
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "urls": [
        "/mcp-turns-tools-into-useful-context/"
      ],
      "docType": "blogPost",
      "template": "blogPost"
    },
    {
      "id": "d060e0ea-da2c-4472-a80e-9f83edd77e7f",
      "name": "MCP makes a content workflow inspectable",
      "path": "WWW / MCP Notes / MCP makes a content workflow inspectable",
      "docTypeId": "0388f06e-e2df-4366-8282-92ea82871671",
      "templateId": "030812a4-3f8a-44b6-a9b1-4f3cb67d9fcd",
      "state": "Published",
      "domains": [],
      "values": [
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.BlockGrid",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "blocks",
          "value": {
            "layout": {
              "Umbraco.BlockGrid": [
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "33000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
                  "settingsKey": null
                }
              ]
            },
            "contentData": [
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "a32337a5-31e5-4664-88c4-3628398541a6",
                "key": "33000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "heading",
                    "value": "MCP makes a content workflow inspectable"
                  },
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextArea",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "intro",
                    "value": "Great automation is not just fast; it is transparent, constrained, and easy to verify."
                  },
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.MediaPicker3",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "image",
                    "value": [
                      {
                        "key": "33000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
                        "mediaKey": "e8b9ec1c-8df8-46e2-a70a-2b93d0a075cb",
                        "mediaTypeAlias": "Image",
                        "crops": [],
                        "focalPoint": null
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.RichText",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "body",
                    "value": {
                      "markup": "<p>MCP is awesome because its tool boundaries make an automated workflow visible. A client asks for a list, a schema, or a targeted update; the server returns a structured response that can be checked before the next step.</p><p>That transparency encourages good habits. Here, the blog was modeled first, content was created second, and every Block Grid payload was read back after saving. The server is not a magic shortcut—it is a reliable surface for deliberate work.</p><p>When teams standardize on those contracts, they can give agents useful capability without giving up the reviewable structure that keeps a site maintainable.</p>",
                      "blocks": {
                        "layout": {},
                        "contentData": [],
                        "settingsData": [],
                        "expose": []
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "settingsData": [],
            "expose": [
